PRD.md — Hedetangen AI Marketing Studio

Version: 1.0
Status: Draft for review
Product: Single-page, client-side AI marketing assistant for Hedetangen AB
Owner: Hedetangen (Joacim & Madeleine)
Build target: Static HTML/CSS/JS deployable on GitHub Pages

---

1. Executive Summary

Hedetangen is a small family-run eco-tourism business in Värmland, Sweden, offering off-grid luxury glamping in a floating AuroraHut on a private island, plus sauna and ice-bath experiences. The owners need marketing, copywriting, social media, and basic business analysis support but have no technical expertise and limited time.

This PRD defines a single-page HTML application where the user chats exclusively with Jennifer, an orchestrator AI persona. Jennifer delegates tasks to predefined expert roles (Copywriter, Marketing Strategist, Social Media Strategist, Business & Pricing Analyst, Visual Director, Researcher) and invokes tools such as web search when needed. The app runs entirely in the browser, stores data locally in IndexedDB/localStorage, and uses the user's own API keys for Groq, OpenRouter, or OpenAI. The design is mobile-first, minimalist Scandinavian, and the entire application can be deployed as static files on GitHub Pages.

---

2. Problem & Opportunity

Problem: Hedetangen's owners are operators, not marketers. They have a compelling brand and a unique product but lack the time, structure, and specialized knowledge to consistently produce high-quality marketing content, run campaigns, and analyze pricing and demand. Generic AI chatbots require prompt engineering skills and produce off-brand, generic luxury imagery and copy that violates the brand's honesty rule.

Opportunity: A purpose-built, brand-aware AI studio lowers the barrier to effective marketing. By embedding Hedetangen's Brand DNA into every expert prompt and providing a guided, chat-based workflow, the owners can generate on-brand ads, captions, campaign plans, and research briefs in minutes — without learning prompt engineering or managing multiple AI tools.

---

3. Goals & Success Metrics

Goal Metric Target (v1)
Zero-friction onboarding Time from first open to first successful AI response < 3 minutes (with API key)
Brand-safe output User-reported "on-brand" rate for generated copy/visual briefs ≥ 90%
Task completion Campaign brief or ad variant set generated in a single session ≥ 70% of sessions
Reliability Successful API calls without unhandled errors ≥ 98% (excluding provider outages)
Owner confidence Qualitative: owners feel comfortable using the tool without technical help "Yes" in post-use survey

---

4. Target Users & Personas

Primary user: Joacim & Madeleine, founders/operators of Hedetangen.

· Small business owners, not marketers.
· Comfortable with everyday apps (Instagram, booking platforms) but not with API keys or prompt engineering.
· Time-poor; need outputs they can use immediately.
· Deeply protective of the brand's authenticity and the "honesty rule."

Secondary user (future): A hired marketing freelancer or family member helping with seasonal campaigns.

---

5. Brand & Design Principles

5.1 Brand DNA (non-negotiable)

The following is the canonical brand context. Every expert system prompt must include a condensed version of these rules, and Jennifer must verify outputs against them.

· Honesty Rule (highest priority): Never depict or imply the real Hedetangen place, AuroraHut, sauna, island, or accommodation unless a reference photo is supplied. Without a reference, generate only generic atmosphere scenes: water, light, fire, textures, hands, natural details, food and drink.
· Essence: Genuine, understated luxury in raw Swedish nature. Rustic luxury, never glamorous luxury. Nothing staged.
· Materials: Solid wood with visible grain, stone, rope, leather, linen, wool, sheepskin, glass, weathered bronze/copper.
· Colour & light: Warm earth tones (deep wood, forest green, moss, bronze, copper, cream, charcoal, soft gold); natural cool tones in winter, dusk, water; golden hour, blue hour, firelight, lantern glow, mist, reflections. Soft natural light only.
· People: At most one person, relaxed and real, often just hands or feet. Never posed, never model-like. Faces not required.
· Cinema: High-end Scandinavian nature cinematography, photorealistic. Single continuous slow camera move (or static), shallow depth of field, tactile close-ups, natural motion. Each shot expresses one sensory feeling.
· Emotion: Serenity, presence, warmth, discovery. Authenticity over perfection.
· Avoid: Invented structures/locations, generic luxury (marble, champagne buckets), plastic, neon, oversaturated look, urban settings, crowds, fast cuts, music, text, logos, watermarks, zoom loops.

5.2 Design language

· Minimalist Scandinavian: generous whitespace, muted warm neutrals, one accent colour (soft bronze/copper), clean sans-serif typography (system fonts for performance), subtle borders, no gradients or shadows except for functional separation.
· Mobile-first: single-column layout on small screens; a two-column layout on desktop (chat + side panel).
· Chat as primary interface: the composer is always visible; expert activity is shown as subtle inline badges (e.g., "Jennifer → Copywriter") rather than separate screens.
· Progressive disclosure: advanced settings (API keys, model selection, temperature, machine prompt) live behind a toggle panel or a settings drawer.

---

6. Core Features

6.1 Jennifer — Orchestrator Persona

· Identity: Warm, competent, concise. Speaks as a trusted marketing partner, not a chatbot.
· Responsibilities:
  · Greet the user and clarify the task if underspecified.
  · Decide which expert(s) to invoke based on the request.
  · Pass relevant context (Brand DNA, prior outputs, user constraints) to experts.
  · Synthesize expert outputs into a coherent response.
  · Invoke tools (web search, content library save) when appropriate.
  · Enforce the Brand DNA honesty rule before returning any output.
· Transparency: Jennifer announces delegation inline: "I'll have our Copywriter draft three Instagram captions, then I'll run them past the Brand Guardrails." No hidden multi-step process.

6.2 Predefined Expert Roles (CRUD)

Users can create, read, update, and delete experts. Each expert has:

Field Description Example
id UUID exp_copy_01
name Display name "Copywriter"
role Short role description "Conversion-focused copy for hospitality and experiences"
systemPrompt Full system prompt, including Brand DNA injection See Appendix B
temperature Default temperature override (optional) 0.7
enabled Whether Jennifer can delegate to this expert true
tags For organization ["copy", "social"]

Seed experts (v1):

1. Copywriter — Ads, captions, landing page copy, email subject lines.
2. Marketing Strategist — Campaign structure, positioning, audience segmentation, channel mix.
3. Social Media Strategist — Platform-specific content calendars, hashtag strategy, engagement prompts.
4. Business & Pricing Analyst — Pricing scenarios, seasonality, occupancy analysis, campaign ROI estimation. Scoped to micro-business decisions; not macroeconomics.
5. Visual Director — Image/video prompts and shot lists that strictly follow the Brand DNA honesty rule.
6. Researcher — Web search synthesis for competitors, trends, local events, and market context. Uses the web-search tool; does not generate copy.

6.3 Provider Integration

The user selects one provider per session (or can switch in settings). The app stores the API key encrypted and never transmits it anywhere except directly to the chosen provider's API endpoint.

Groq (default for development)

· Endpoint: https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions (OpenAI-compatible).
· On API key entry, fetch GET /openai/v1/models and filter for chat-capable models.
· Display model list with known context windows and free-tier limits (curated metadata for v1; optional live metadata later).
· Example free models (as of late 2025/2026): llama-3.3-70b-versatile, llama-3.1-8b-instant, openai/gpt-oss-120b, moonshotai/kimi-k2-instruct. Limit list to models that support chat completions.

OpenRouter

· Endpoint: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions.
· Model list: GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models. Filter for models where pricing.prompt === "0" and pricing.completion === "0" (free models). Example free models: deepseek/deepseek-r1:free, meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free, qwen/qwen-2.5-72b-instruct:free.
· Note: Free model availability changes frequently; display a "last refreshed" timestamp.

OpenAI

· Endpoint: https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions.
· Model list: GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models. OpenAI generally does not offer free models; the user is responsible for billing. Display a warning that usage incurs cost.
· The app should never assume a free model exists for OpenAI; the model selector should list all available models with a "paid" badge.

Error handling: Map provider errors to user-friendly messages. For 429 (rate limit), Jennifer suggests an alternative model or a retry delay. For 401 (invalid key), show a clear prompt to re-enter the key in settings.

6.4 Chat Interface

· Message list with role labels: You, Jennifer, and inline expert tags (e.g., "Copywriter").
· Markdown rendering for AI responses (headers, lists, bold, links). Code blocks for JSON export previews.
· Streaming responses (where provider supports SSE) with a typing indicator.
· Copy button on each AI message; "Save to Library" action.
· Inline tool activity: e.g., "🔍 Jennifer is searching the web for competitor glamping pricing…"
· Message persistence in IndexedDB; chat history survives reloads.
· Clear chat / new session button (with confirmation).

6.5 Content Library

· Automatically saves any message the user marks with "Save to Library."
· Jennifer can also save outputs proactively (e.g., after a campaign brief) with a note.
· Fields: id, title, content, type (copy/campaign/research/visual-brief), tags, createdAt, sourceChatId.
· Filter by type and tag; search by text.
· Export selected items or entire library as JSON.

6.6 Guided Campaign Builder (Wizard Mode)

An optional, three-step guided flow accessible from a "+" button in the composer:

1. Objective & Audience: Select goal (awareness / bookings / off-season / local partnerships), target segment (couples, international travelers, locals, corporate retreats), and language (SV / EN / bilingual).
2. Channel & Format: Select channel(s) (Instagram, Facebook, email, website, Google Ads) and desired output (captions, ad variants, email sequence, landing page sections, visual brief).
3. Brand Guardrails Review: A read-only card summarizing the Brand DNA rules that will apply. User can toggle "Strict mode" (default on) which forces the honesty rule and material/colour constraints.

Jennifer then orchestrates the appropriate experts and returns a structured brief with variants. The wizard inputs are also passed as context to the chat so the user can iterate conversationally afterwards.

6.7 Settings Panel (Advanced)

Toggled via a gear icon; hidden by default.

Setting Description
Provider Groq / OpenRouter / OpenAI
API Key Masked input; stored encrypted in IndexedDB. Never displayed in plain text after save.
Model Dropdown populated from the provider's model list. Search/filter. Show free/paid badge and context window if known.
Temperature Slider 0.0–1.5 (default 0.7 for copy, 0.4 for research). Per-expert override optional.
Machine Prompt Optional global system prompt appended after the Brand DNA injection. Useful for seasonal campaigns.
Language preference SV / EN / Auto.
Brand Guardrails Link to edit the Brand DNA block (see 6.8).
Import / Export Buttons for JSON import/export of experts, settings (excluding keys), library, and guardrails.
Clear all data Destructive action with typed confirmation.

6.8 Brand Guardrails Editor

A dedicated panel (or modal) where the owner can edit the canonical Brand DNA block. Changes apply immediately to all subsequent expert calls. Include:

· A "Reset to default" button.
· A warning if the honesty rule is removed or weakened: "The honesty rule protects your brand from AI hallucinations. Are you sure you want to remove it?"
· Version history (last 5 edits) stored locally.

6.9 Import / Export (JSON)

· Export: Produces a single .json file containing:
  · schemaVersion
  · experts (array)
  · guardrails (Brand DNA object)
  · library (array)
  · settings (excluding API keys; model preference may be included)
  · exportedAt
· Import: Validates schema, shows a preview of what will be imported, and lets the user choose merge vs. replace. API keys are never included in export files.
· Expert-only import/export is also available from the expert editor for quick sharing.

