7. Technical Architecture

7.1 Constraints

· Single-page HTML application. No server-side runtime. Deployable to GitHub Pages (static hosting).
· No build step required for v1 (or minimal, optional build). Prefer native ES modules and vanilla JavaScript to reduce complexity. A tiny reactive library (e.g., Alpine.js via CDN) is acceptable if it materially speeds development, but plain JS is preferred for longevity.
· Mobile-first responsive design.
· All data stays in the browser except API calls directly to the chosen provider.

7.2 Storage Strategy

Data Storage Encryption
API keys IndexedDB AES-GCM via Web Crypto API; encryption key stored as a non-extractable CryptoKey in IndexedDB
Chat messages IndexedDB Plaintext (local only)
Experts IndexedDB Plaintext (exportable)
Guardrails / Brand DNA IndexedDB Plaintext (exportable)
Content library IndexedDB Plaintext (exportable)
UI preferences (theme, last model) localStorage N/A

Important: API keys are encrypted at rest but decrypted in memory only when making a provider call. The app never logs keys to the console. A prominent notice in settings states: "Your API key is stored only in this browser, encrypted. It is sent directly to [Provider] when you chat. It is never sent to Hedetangen or any third party."

7.3 Provider Abstraction Layer

A single Provider interface with methods:

· listModels(): Promise<ModelInfo[]>
· chat(messages, options): AsyncGenerator<StreamChunk> (or Promise for non-streaming fallback)
· validateKey(): Promise<boolean>

Implementations: GroqProvider, OpenRouterProvider, OpenAIProvider, MockProvider (for demo mode).

All provider calls go through a request wrapper that:

· Adds the correct auth headers.
· Handles timeouts (AbortController).
· Maps errors to a normalized AIError type.
· Never logs the API key.

7.4 Orchestration Flow (Simplified)

```
User message
    ↓
Jennifer (system prompt + Brand DNA + conversation history)
    ↓
Decision: respond directly OR delegate to expert(s) OR invoke tool
    ↓
If expert: call provider with expert system prompt + context
    ↓
If tool: web search (via provider-native tool or a search API) → synthesize
    ↓
Jennifer reviews output against Brand DNA guardrails
    ↓
Stream final response to UI
    ↓
Optionally save to library
```

Note on web search: Groq and OpenRouter may offer tool-calling / web-search capabilities depending on the model. For v1, Jennifer can perform web research by instructing a capable model to use its knowledge and by allowing the user to paste URLs for analysis. Native web-search tool integration is a v1.1 enhancement if provider support is reliable. The Researcher expert can still synthesize information the user provides or that the model already knows, with clear caveats about recency.

7.5 Deployment

· Static files: index.html, styles.css, app.js, providers.js, storage.js, experts.js, guardrails.js.
· GitHub Pages: deploy from main branch /root or /docs.
· Optional: a simple 404.html that redirects to index.html for client-side routing (if any).
· No environment variables; all configuration is user-supplied via the UI.

